# Region selector. Check in each look.
setup foot -T A & foot -T B &
wait 3
rec rs-first 1 ipc screen region screenshot
note Dim and hint appear no later in Rust than in QML (+-1 frame): the first selection must be immediate.
wait 1
ptr move 400 300 sleep 200 down glide 900 650 400
shot rs-drag
note Dim outside the rectangle 400..900 x 300..650; outline square (1 px white / 2 px primary); readout "500 x 350" at about (908,658). Compare QML vs Rust. NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness.
rec rs-up 1 ptr move 400 300 down glide 900 650 200 up
note On release the overlay goes at once and the screenshot thumbnail appears about 160 ms later (QML vs Rust).
wait 2
ipc shotEditor close
ipc screen region ocr
wait 1
ptr glide 700 400 150
wait 1
shot rs-window
note Pointer over a window: its rect outlined (r 12 Glass / 16 Material), the rest dimmed; hint "Drag to select an area to copy text, or click a window. Esc to cancel."
key -k Escape
wait 1
shot rs-esc
note Escape removes the overlay completely.
ipc screen circle
wait 1
rec rs-circle 2 ptr move 800 500 down glide 1000 400 150 glide 1200 500 150 glide 1000 650 150 glide 800 520 150
note Circle to search: the stroke has a glow, no box and no size readout while drawing. The search itself needs the network and is not testable here; the Rust log should show screen.captured ["circle", ...].
shot rs-circle-shot
note Stroke and glow still visible (button held); no rectangle or size.
ptr move 960 540 up
wait 1
ipc screen region screenshot
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
shot rs-keys-esc
note After Escape the overlay is gone.
ipc screen region screenshot
wait 1
key -k Return
wait 2
shot rs-keys-return
note Return captures the whole screen (the screenshot thumbnail appears).
ipc shotEditor close
# MANUAL: Right button at (960,540) while the selector is open (the pointer helper has no right button)
# MANUAL: Circle search result (no network): check the Rust log for screen.captured
